From d9b32be5e77cb27be3c0831858c08c7fb1907670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prasanna A P <106952318+Prasanna721@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 22:16:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] console + errors: per-tab buffer routed by CDP session_id

Move EventTracker from DaemonState into PageInfo so each tab owns its own
console + uncaught-exception ring. CDP loop routes Runtime.consoleAPICalled
and Runtime.exceptionThrown by event.session_id into the matching page,
bypassing the active-session filter so background tabs are captured too.
Iframes (sessions that don't match any page) drop on the floor for now.

handle_console / handle_errors accept an optional "tab": <id> in the cmd
JSON; with no tab, they fall back to the active page (REPL parity).
"console --clear" now drains: returns messages then clears the buffer,
matching how every external poller (preprint included) actually uses it.
Adds --tab <N> | t<N> to both CLI parsers.
